{"name":"Cityscape","hex":"#dae3e7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cityscape","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The view of the buildings of a city, usually referring to a pictured landscape."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cityscape"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cityscape","blocks":[{"text":"In the visual arts, a cityscape is an artistic representation, such as a painting, drawing, print or photograph, of the physical aspects of a city or urban area. It is the urban equivalent of a landscape. Townscape is roughly synonymous with cityscape, though it implies the same difference in urban size and density implicit in the difference between the words city and town. In urban design the terms refer to the configuration of built forms and interstitial space."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/The_Dam_in_Amsterdam%2C_by_Gerrit_Adriaensz_Berckheyde.jpg/330px-The_Dam_in_Amsterdam%2C_by_Gerrit_Adriaensz_Berckheyde.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cityscape"},{"title":"Cityscape (horse)","blocks":[{"text":"Cityscape is a British-bred Thoroughbred racehorse and sire, who raced in England, Ireland, Hong Kong, France, Dubai, Canada and Italy and was twice rated among the top 40 racehorses in the world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Owner_Mr_K_Abdulla.svg/330px-Owner_Mr_K_Abdulla.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cityscape_(horse)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Dresden_photochrom2.jpg/500px-Dresden_photochrom2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Dresden_photochrom2.jpg/1280px-Dresden_photochrom2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=t